window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["08"]={"https://theconversation.com/how-lula-turned-the-tables-on-the-right-in-brazil-and-the-us-with-his-comeback-presidential-victory-294810":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"619b933b748841eb25721433fe31cfc72e05c3289165dcb80e683683a78a1994","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-lula-turned-the-tables-on-the-right-in-brazil-and-the-us-with-his-comeback-presidential-victory-294810","bytes":191816,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How Lula turned the tables on the right in Brazil and the US with his comeback presidential victory","by":[{"n":"Anthony W. Pereira","r":"Executive Director of the Stone Center for Latin American Studies, Tulane University; King's College London"}],"pub":"2026-10-26T22:15:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A leader who stood up to U.S. President Donald Trump just won an election in Latin America’s biggest country, reversing a ",["trend of new right-wing governments","https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/10/24/latin-americas-maga-wave-is-widening-trumps-political-military-reach/"]," in the region over the past two years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incumbent Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, ",["having narrowly lost","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/06/keeping-up-with-the-bolsonaros-flavios-surprise-first-round-election-win-heralds-rise-of-a-political-dynasty"]," to Flávio Bolsonaro in the first round of voting on Oct. 5, 2026, staged a remarkable comeback on Oct. 25. He erased the deficit and won the ",["all-important runoff election","https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-2026-live-second-round-results"]," by more than 3.5 percentage points – more than 4 million votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was a stunning result for the leader who proved to be the first Brazilian candidate to win a presidential election after not winning the first round, and who had been all but written off for a possible win. As a ",["professor of Latin American politics","https://stonecenter.tulane.edu/anthony-w-pereira"],", I believe the result offers a number of key political lessons for Brazil, Latin America – and even the United States."]},{"k":"h","s":["A contest of worldviews — and social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["The choice in the second-round election was stark. Lula offered measures to ameliorate steep income inequalities and an economy built on a transition to clean energy, environmental protection and increased access to higher education and technical training. On international matters, Lula balanced defending Brazilian sovereignty from a Trump administration ",["keen on meddling in Latin America","https://theconversation.com/trumps-coercive-tactics-in-latin-america-evoke-era-of-gunboat-diplomacy-and-the-rise-of-anti-imperialism-it-helped-spur-279238"],", and maintaining good relations with an array of nations and blocs, including the European Union and China."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolsonaro, meanwhile, promised sweeping cuts to government spending, more militarized policing and eager support for the Trump administration’s ",["campaign against drug violence","https://theconversation.com/trumps-narco-terrorism-war-in-latin-america-evokes-reagan-then-as-now-its-more-about-fighting-leftists-than-drug-runners-284287"],". His pitch also came with offers to U.S. investors ",["of access to critical minerals","https://atlasinstitute.org/flavio-bolsonaros-washington-visit-highlights-security-minerals-and-diplomatic-tensions-between-brazil-and-the-us/"]," in Brazil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such right-wing populism has been ascendant in Latin America of late, and Lula also had to overcome an anti-incumbent mood, brought on by high prices, stagnant salaries, steep interest rates and a ",["massive corruption scandal","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/how-an-obscure-banker-slipped-into-brazils-political-inner-circle-triggering-2026-03-13/"]," involving Brazilian elites. That banking probe directly ",["ensnared Bolsonaro himself","https://www.intercept.com.br/2026/05/13/audio-flavio-negociou-vorcaro-milhoes/"],", as well as powerful Supreme Court justice Alexandre de Moraes, whom Bolsonaro’s supporters ",["had tried to link","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/scandal-brazil-court-jair-flavio-bolsonaro-power-election-moraes-lula"]," to Lula."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lula also had to neuter a social media landscape that has been ",["dominated by images","https://apublica.org/sentinela/2022/10/no-2o-turno-bolsonaro-aposta-em-fake-news-que-liga-lula-ao-crime-organizado/"]," and ",["narratives","https://veja.abril.com.br/politica/tse-manda-flavio-e-apoiadores-excluirem-videos-falsos-de-uso-de-drogas-em-ato-pro-lula/"]," disparaging the president and his Workers’ Party."]},{"k":"p","s":["Right-wing ",["dominance of that online ecosystem","https://www.meioemensagem.com.br/marketing/eleicao-de-bolsonaro-marca-mudanca-no-marketing-politico"]," ",["helped carry","https://www.scielo.br/j/rbcpol/a/TsmbKCcpgQW8dRWLNd8vfZR/abstract/?lang=pt"]," Jair Bolsonaro, the 2026 hopeful’s father, to power in 2018 and got him close to reelection in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Especially after the first-round results in the 2026 vote, many analysts assumed the same ",["pro-Bolsonaro social media presence","https://g1.globo.com/politica/eleicoes/2026/noticia/2026/10/09/disputa-digital-lula-reune-jovens-influenciadores-eleitos-e-aliados-de-flavio-organizam-reacao-nas-redes.ghtml"]," would once again be hegemonic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead, after the first round, a network of young, tech-savvy pro-Lula communicators created and shared effective, often amusing videos on WhatsApp and Instagram."]},{"k":"p","s":["And they appealed to the center and even some of the right. All told, Lula easily made up more than 2 million votes by which he lost in the first round. He didn’t just increase turnout by millions and lower abstention rates; he also saw the state with the country’s second-largest electorate, Minas Gerais, ",["flip to his side entirely","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/10/26/americas/brazil-election-results-takeaways-latam-hk-intl"]," – a swing of nearly 700,000 votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emblematic of the strength of the campaign was the growth in subscribers to the ",["WhatsApp channel Lula’s Army","https://www.bbc.com/portuguese/articles/c678pegn3krmo"],", which grew from 50,000 on Oct. 5 to more than 10 million by the night of the historic election."]},{"k":"p","s":["The creator of the channel, André Janones, is a federal deputy for the Rede Party, an ally of the Workers’ Party, and a rising star in the circle around Lula. Likewise, Ana Elisa Santos Silva, a 21-year-old ",["digital influencer and law student","https://g1.globo.com/mg/centro-oeste/eleicoes/2026/noticia/2026/10/05/quem-e-ana-elisa-influenciadora-eleita-deputada-mais-jovem-de-mg.ghtml"]," in the Workers’ Party, got the most votes of any federal deputy in the swing state of Minas Gerais."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cracks in the ‘Americanization’ theory of politics"]},{"k":"p","s":["A prevalent narrative of Brazilian politics has held that the country’s divisions increasingly mirror those of the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of that idea is due to Trump’s loss in the 2020 election and the resulting attack on the U.S. Capitol on Jan. 6, 2021, which ",["eerily presaged events","https://korbel.du.edu/resource/how-us-capitol-insurrection-influenced-jan-8-violence-in-brazil/"]," following Jair Bolsanaro’s 2022 loss."]},{"k":"p","s":["Like in the U.S., there has also been a rapid rise of a ",["politically active evangelical right","https://aeon.co/essays/what-will-an-evangelical-brazil-look-like"]," in Brazil."]},{"k":"p","s":["More fundamentally, proponents of the ",["Americanization thesis","https://bahiaeconomica.com.br/economia-e-politica/sonho-do-proprio-negocio-atinge-41-dos-brasileiros-209776"]," hold that U.S.-style deindustrialization and “Uberization” of the Brazilian economy have led to a decline of the unionized working class – a core support base for the left – and its replacement by an army of gig employees ",["dreaming of owning their own businesses","https://tribunademinas.com.br/maistendencias/ter-o-proprio-negocio-ou-garantir-os-direitos-da-carteira-assinada-pesquisa-revela-qual-caminho-os-brasileiros-mais-associam-a-uma-vida-melhor#goog_rewarded"]," and throwing off the shackles of the taxing and regulating state."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet similarities between the two countries shouldn’t be confused for politics always moving on parallel tracks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Survey ",["research suggests","https://iclnoticias.com.br/economia/maioria-brasileiros-estado-ipsos/"]," that many Brazilians see the ",["state as responsible","https://multivix.edu.br/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/o-estado-como-garantidor-dos-direitos-sociais.pdf"]," for the realization of their constitutionally protected social rights, including healthcare, education and pensions. Many also regard government employment as inherently more stable and dignified than the harsh labor markets of the private sector, especially for the relatively unskilled."]},{"k":"p","s":["For all of the apparent rise in American-style libertarian politics in Brazil, the reality is that such a viewpoint remains much smaller in the country. Flávio Bolsonaro’s bet, like his father’s before him, was that this strain of libertarian right-wing politics could nonetheless propel him to victory, ",["much as it apparently had for Javier Milei","https://ffms.pt/pt-pt/atualmentes/argentina-elegeu-o-primeiro-presidente-liberal-libertario-da-historia-da-humanidade"]," in Argentina in 2023. But it was not enough."]},{"k":"h","s":["One election can’t fix deep polarization"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even with Lula’s win, Flávio Bolsonaro’s Liberal Party did exceptionally well at the legislative level."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the next Brazilian Congress convenes on Feb. 1, 2027, the ",["Liberal Party will control","https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/right-wing-wave-brazils-congress-boosts-bolsonaro-camp-ahead-presidential-runoff-2026-10-05/"]," 28 seats in the Senate – 35% of the total; and 121 seats in the lower house – 24% of the total (as well as five governorships, which are 19% of the total)."]},{"k":"p","s":["When factoring in expected Liberal Party allies, it is clear that the right will have bigger majorities in both houses for Lula’s next administration. That will help ",["Congress solidify","https://sumauma.com/por-que-o-congresso-ganhou-tanto-poder-e-por-que-isso-torna-mais-dificil-renova-lo/"]," control vis-a-vis the executive branch in terms of legislation and, crucially, the budget."]},{"k":"h","s":["A series of unknowns facing Lula"]},{"k":"p","s":["The election raises several questions."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, it is unclear how Lula, who will turn 81 on Oct. 27, will be able to effectively govern. The president will have to make major concessions to a Congress with little capacity for responsibly delivering coherent policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The federal Supreme Court is also seen as politicized, fragmented and tainted by scandals. On the other hand, Lula ",["could appoint","https://g1.globo.com/politica/noticia/2026/10/26/reeleito-lula-pode-indicar-mais-4-ministros-para-o-stf-no-proximo-mandato.ghtml"]," four new Supreme Court justices because of upcoming retirements, meaning that he could shape the country’s highest judicial body in a way that enhances his ability to manage Congress."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet it might be difficult for Lula to simultaneously meet the demands coming from Congress and those from the business community. For example, many will push the government to curb the fiscal deficit, currently running at a ",["very high annual level","https://www.ft.com/content/bffe028e-838d-4e74-b05e-62f6db4978db?syn-25a6b1a6=1"]," of close to 8% of gross domestic product."]},{"k":"p","s":["A second question is whether Bolsonaro’s loss will splinter the right. One interpretation of the 2026 election is that to be competitive, the right will want to move on from the Bolsonaro family. One potential figure is Tarcísio de Freitas, a former cabinet member in the Jair Bolsonaro government and popular governor of São Paulo. Yet there are nonetheless five members of the Bolsonaro family in the new Congress, and they are likely to try to keep together the coalition that fought for Flávio Bolsonaro’s campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, it’s not clear how the Trump administration, which ",["interfered decisively against Lula’s agenda","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/us-trump-rubio-meddling-brazil-election"],", will react to his win – and to what extent it will support Bolsonaro’s denial of his election loss even though it was bigger than his father’s in 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whatever the extent of any interference, the Trump administration’s right-wing Latin American vision invariably sets up conflict with Lula. Yet while the Trump preference was always for Flávio Bolsonaro, that doesn’t mean his administration won’t pragmatically engage with Lula ",["even as it pressures","https://theconversation.com/how-a-diplomatic-snub-evokes-the-complicated-us-brazil-relationship-in-the-second-trump-era-278649"]," his government. For his part, Lula continues to hold his own leverage, including through Brazil’s ",["large deposits of rare earth elements","https://www.bbc.com/portuguese/articles/cglpyzegwkko"]," that the Trump administration covets."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the past eight years of Brazilian politics are any guide, Lula’s next administration is likely to be a turbulent one in which enduring ",["divisions at home and abroad","https://cebri.org/br/midia/710/riscos-globais-em-2026-e-implicacoes-para-o-posicionamento-estrategico-do-brasil"]," are continually tested."]}],"chars":8346},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"dbfde540fbc5e6dd42553ece893b68ca47f8e7df1a2737cd823b8a666e71ba8d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/germany","bytes":80201,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Germany travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:05+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Germany set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["German Embassy in the UK","https://uk.diplo.de/uk-en/01/embassy/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Germany follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a residence permit, you must have a valid passport for the duration of your stay. Renew it before the expiry date."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Germany, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-germany-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At German border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the German government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or permit you need with the ",["German Embassy in the UK","https://uk.diplo.de/uk-en/02/visa/-/2449340"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Germany with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-germany#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["A temporary reintroduction of border controls is currently in place at Germany’s land borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["See information from ",["The Federal Ministry of the Interior and Community","https://www.bmi.bund.de/SharedDocs/pressemitteilungen/EN/2024/09/binnengrenzkontrollen_en.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checkpoints on the Germany/Poland border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Poland has introduced border checks on the Germany/Poland border. Vehicles may be stopped and documentation checked. For further information see ",["Poland Travel Advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/poland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Germany guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/88/germany#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into and out of Germany","https://www.zoll.de/EN/Private-individuals/Travel/Entering-Germany/Duties-and-taxes/Travellers-allowances/travellers-allowances_node.html"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Germany"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Germany"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare any amount above 10,000 euros in cash or other payment types. You can find more information on the ",["German Federal Foreign Office website.","https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/-/2144094"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Germany"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Germany."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in public places visited by foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["markets"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship and religious sites, including synagogues"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places and public gatherings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in July 2026, 1 person was killed and 29 injured when a vehicle drove into crowds celebrating Christopher Street Day, Berlin’s annual LGBT+ Pride event"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2024, 3 people were killed and several injured following a knife attack in Solingen"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2021, 5 people were stabbed and injured on a train in Neumarkt, Bavaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020, one person was killed and another seriously injured in a knife attack in Dresden"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020, 8 people were killed and 5 injured in 2 mass shootings in shisha bars in Hanau"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2019, 2 people were shot and killed after a failed attempt to enter a synagogue in the eastern German city of Halle"]},{"k":"p","s":["German authorities regularly report that they have disrupted planned attacks and made arrests."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are similar to the UK. Take sensible precautions to avoid mugging, bag-snatching and pickpocketing. Be particularly vigilant at airports, railway stations and in crowded public places or gatherings. Do not leave bags unattended."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Counterfeit currency"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only change money at banks, ATMs or official money exchanges. Check your change when paying in cash. British nationals have been arrested for trying to pay with counterfeit currency."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s not a legal requirement to carry ID. However, if you cannot show ID when asked, police can escort you to get your passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["They will ask for a passport and, if you are a resident, for your residence card as well."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Germany have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re taking part in organised outdoor activities, check that the company is reputable and has documented safety procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["For sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and for sports classed as particularly dangerous (for example off-piste skiing, mountain biking, climbing or paragliding), your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your country of residence or possible transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check weather forecasts and conditions and make sure you’re properly equipped for the worst-case scenario with items such as a map, compass, GPS and telecommunication equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Risks are greater if you undertake any activity alone. You may want to hire a guide for expert advice. Always leave copies of your itinerary with someone."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Winter sports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["preparing for winter sports abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take advice on weather and avalanche conditions before you travel. Follow local skiing laws and regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Off-piste skiing is very dangerous and can invalidate your travel insurance. Avalanches are a risk in some areas. Follow safety instructions carefully and go with a qualified guide. Check ahead on the ",["European Avalanche Warning Service","https://www.avalanches.org/"]," website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Germany, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Germany guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/germany/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Germany for up to 6 months with your UK photocard driving licence. If you stay longer, you’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["German Federal Transport Ministry","https://www.bmvi.de/SharedDocs/EN/Articles/StV/Roadtraffic/validity-foreign-driving-licences-in-germany.html"]," has more information on the validity of non-German driving licences."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re driving a vehicle that does not belong to you, you may need to show written permission from the registered owner."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-symbols-and-identifiers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Germany, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in Germany, check the ",["driving requirements for residents","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-germany#driving-in-germany"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Low emission zones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some inner-city areas have an environmental zone (‘Umweltzone’). Only vehicles that meet specific exhaust emission standards can enter. See ",["Federal Ministry for the Environment, Nature Conservation, Nuclear Safety and Consumer Protection","https://www.bmuv.de/en/topics/air-noise-mobility/air/emissions-control-sticker-low-emission-zone"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel, check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Germany","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/88/germany#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Germany","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/88/germany"],", including Mpox."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Germany, including mountainous regions. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Germany"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/germany-list-of-medical-practitionersfacilities"],", where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Germany, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-germany"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Germany"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you’re involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Germany"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Germany"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Germany"]," in Germany"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-germany?utm_source=british-embassy-berlin&utm_medium=embassy&utm_campaign=germany"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/germany-prisoner-pack/information-pack-for-british-nationals-arrested-or-detained-in-germany"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/germany/british-embassy-berlin"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Germany","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-germany"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16168,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/salah-sebut-salah-nasib-label-keliru-tentara-bayaran-bagi-wni-di-militer-rusia-292982":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"b7ac30ac5726bfb5c7ce8cdcaa9657a1cfc7efa135b0ca635cb6b057a7ca1b9c","read":"https://theconversation.com/salah-sebut-salah-nasib-label-keliru-tentara-bayaran-bagi-wni-di-militer-rusia-292982","bytes":183871,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Salah sebut, salah nasib: Label keliru ‘tentara bayaran’ bagi WNI di militer Rusia","by":[{"n":"Radityo Dharmaputra","r":"Lecturer in Foreign Policy Analysis, Russia-Eastern European-Eurasian Studies, Department of International Relations, Universitas Airlangga, Universitas Airlangga"}],"pub":"2026-10-01T11:57:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Label ‘tentara bayaran’ tidak selalu tepat secara hukum bagi WNI di militer Rusia."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Istilah tersebut menjadi bagian dari perang narasi Rusia-Ukraina."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Pelabelan ini dapat berdampak pada perlindungan hukum WNI yang tertangkap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seorang pemuda asal Natuna, Kepulauan Riau, ",["tewas","https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20260928143927-20-1409071/diduga-pemuda-natuna-jadi-tentara-rusia-tewas-oleh-drone-ukraina"]," —diduga akibat serangan drone Ukraina di Rusia pada 20 September 2026. Pemuda berusia 30 tahun itu sebelumnya bekerja sebagai teknisi listrik di Filipina."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut keluarganya, ia diduga direkrut agen secara tidak resmi untuk bekerja di bagian logistik militer Rusia. Pemberitaan tentang kematiannya menyebut pemuda itu sebagai ‘tentara bayaran’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Istilah tersebut melekat pada WNI di militer Rusia setelah Dinas Intelijen Luar Negeri Ukraina (SZRU) pada 27 Agustus ",["mengumumkan","https://szru.gov.ua/en/news-media/news/the-kremlin-is-looking-for-new-cannon-fodder-on-the-islands-of-indonesia"]," telah memeroleh dokumen tentang delapan WNI yang disebut direkrut ke dalam militer Rusia. Sejak itu, ",["sejumlah media","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/09/02/09411651/8-wni-jadi-tentara-bayaran-rusia-diiming-imingi-gaji-besar-berujung-ke-medan"]," dan ",["pejabat","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5748464/duta-besar-ri-di-moskow-imbau-waspada-jebakan-tentara-bayaran"]," menggunakan istilah ‘tentara bayaran’ untuk menyebut mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Tewasnya Prigozhin: apa dampaknya bagi pemerintah Rusia dan nasib perang di Ukraina?","https://theconversation.com/tewasnya-prigozhin-apa-dampaknya-bagi-pemerintah-rusia-dan-nasib-perang-di-ukraina-212445"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Istilah ini memang terdengar masuk akal. Sebab, ",["menurut SZRU","https://szru.gov.ua/en/news-media/news/the-kremlin-is-looking-for-new-cannon-fodder-on-the-islands-of-indonesia"],", perekrutannya bertumpu pada aspek finansial: iming-iming gaji tinggi, pekerjaan nontempur, percepatan kewarganegaraan Rusia, dan tunjangan sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, ‘tentara bayaran’ bukan sekadar istilah untuk orang asing yang berperang demi uang. Dalam hukum humaniter internasional, definisinya jauh lebih spesifik, sehingga istilah itu kurang tepat bagi WNI yang resmi menjadi anggota angkatan bersenjata Rusia. Pemakaiannya juga membawa akibat politik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam perang Rusia-Ukraina, ‘tentara bayaran’ adalah ",["label","https://foreignpolicy.com/2022/03/15/ukraine-war-foreign-fighters-legion-volunteers-legal-status/"]," yang dipakai kedua pihak untuk mendelegitimasi warga asing di barisan lawan. Mengulang label itu berarti ikut mengadopsi narasi perang yang berpotensi mempersempit perlindungan bagi WNI."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tidak semua prajurit asing tentara bayaran"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sejak awal, status para WNI tersebut belum sepenuhnya terverifikasi. Seorang analis keamanan ",["mencatat","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/09/03/10191851/mengapa-wni-tertarik-menjadi-tentara-bayaran-di-negeri-asing"]," bahwa dokumen Ukraina yang beredar merupakan daftar pemrosesan visa turis. Alhasil, ia belum cukup membuktikan seseorang telah ikut bertempur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menteri Koordinator Bidang Hukum, HAM, Imigrasi, dan Pemasyarakatan, Yusril Ihza Mahendra juga ",["menyebut","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5731661/yusril-verifikasi-wni-jadi-tentara-rusia-masih-berproses"]," informasi tersebut masih sepihak."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menariknya, ",["laporan SZRU","https://szru.gov.ua/en/news-media/news/the-kremlin-is-looking-for-new-cannon-fodder-on-the-islands-of-indonesia"]," yang menjadi sumber pemberitaan itu tidak menggunakan kata ",["mercenary (tentara bayaran)","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/international-and-comparative-law-quarterly/article/modern-slavery-in-armed-conflict-foreign-forced-fighters-in-ukraine/1D0028BC9208968FF6A5D50F0C26F008"],". Laporan tersebut menyebut para WNI direkrut ke dalam barisan tentara Rusia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hal ini penting karena Rusia memang memiliki ",["jalur kontrak bagi warga asing","https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2024/01/04/putin-further-eases-citizenship-process-for-foreigners-in-russian-army-a83639"]," untuk menjadi prajurit profesional."]},{"k":"p","s":["Duta Besar Rusia untuk Indonesia, Sergei Tolchenov, ",["mengatakan","https://news.republika.co.id/berita/t1aft6377/dubes-rusia-tak-tahu-eks-marinir-ri-gabung-tentara-moskow-salahkan-satria-soal-hilang-status-warga"]," kontrak tersebut berlaku bagi warga Rusia maupun warga asing. Seorang WNI yang direkrut juga ",["mengaku","https://news.republika.co.id/berita/tlbi3v484/percaya-janji-manis-agen-deden-kini-terjebak-jadi-tentara-rusia"]," menandatangani kontrak selama setahun dalam bahasa Rusia dan sempat ditempatkan di batalion tempur sebelum dipindahkan ke bagian logistik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Putin dilemahkan oleh Wagner – tetapi Ukraina juga melewatkan kesempatan ini","https://theconversation.com/putin-dilemahkan-oleh-wagner-tetapi-ukraina-juga-melewatkan-kesempatan-ini-208672"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam ",["hukum humaniter internasional","https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/api-1977/article-47"],", anggota angkatan bersenjata suatu pihak dalam konflik tidak otomatis menjadi tentara bayaran hanya karena mereka menerima gaji atau merupakan warga negara asing. ",["Protokol Tambahan I Konvensi Jenewa","https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/assets/treaties/470-AP-I-EN.pdf"]," memiliki definisi khusus mengenai tentara bayaran dan mengecualikan anggota angkatan bersenjata dari kategori tersebut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, setiap kasus perlu diperiksa satu per satu. WNI yang resmi menjadi anggota militer Rusia berbeda statusnya dengan orang yang direkrut agen di luar struktur militer."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kasus pemuda Natuna","https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20260928143927-20-1409071/diduga-pemuda-natuna-jadi-tentara-rusia-tewas-oleh-drone-ukraina"],", misalnya, menunjukkan bahwa perekrutan bisa saja terjadi melalui janji pekerjaan di bagian logistik, sehingga status sebenarnya masih perlu dibuktikan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bagian dari perang narasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Istilah ‘tentara bayaran’ tidak digunakan dalam ruang politik yang netral."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada Maret 2024, Kementerian Pertahanan Rusia ",["pernah menyebut","https://news.detik.com/berita/d-7243516/kemlu-ri-respons-klaim-rusia-soal-10-wni-jadi-tentara-bayaran-ukraina/amp"]," 10 WNI sebagai ‘tentara bayaran asing’ yang berperang untuk Ukraina. Empat di antaranya ",["disebut tewas","https://news.detik.com/bbc-world/d-7243236/rusia-klaim-10-wni-jadi-tentara-bayaran-ukraina-4-tewas"],". Klaim tersebut kemudian ",["dibantah Panglima TNI sebagai hoaks","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/4021617/panglima-tni-isu-10-wni-jadi-tentara-bayaran-ukraina-hoaks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kini, ketika muncul ",["laporan mengenai WNI","https://szru.gov.ua/en/news-media/news/the-kremlin-is-looking-for-new-cannon-fodder-on-the-islands-of-indonesia"]," di pihak Rusia, Ukraina menggunakan bingkai serupa. SZRU menyebut Kremlin sedang mencari ‘umpan meriam’ baru di Indonesia. Sementara Kedutaan Besar Rusia membalas dengan menuduh Ukraina aktif ",["merekrut tentara bayaran asing","https://t.me/kedubesrusia/4473"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan kata lain, kedua pihak menggunakan istilah tersebut untuk menggambarkan warga asing yang berada di barisan lawan. Namun, posisi keduanya tidak setara. Rusia adalah pihak yang melakukan agresi, dan Indonesia ",["memberikan suara setuju","https://www.un.org/sites/un2.un.org/files/voting_rec_a-es-11-l.1.pdf"]," pada ",["resolusi Majelis Umum PBB Maret 2022","https://news.un.org/en/story/2022/03/1113152"]," yang menuntut Rusia menarik seluruh pasukannya dari Ukraina."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi Indonesia yang bukan pihak dalam perang, penggunaan istilah semacam ini perlu dilakukan dengan hati-hati, terutama ketika yang dibicarakan adalah warga Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Bagaimana seharusnya Indonesia bersikap terhadap konflik Rusia-Ukraina?","https://theconversation.com/bagaimana-seharusnya-indonesia-bersikap-terhadap-konflik-rusia-ukraina-178152"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Label menentukan perlakuan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalannya jadi makin serius ketika seseorang ditangkap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Status ‘tentara bayaran’ memiliki konsekuensi berbeda dalam hukum perang dibandingkan anggota angkatan bersenjata. Protokol Tambahan I ",["tidak memberikan status tawanan perang","https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/api-1977/article-47"]," kepada tentara bayaran, sementara ",["Konvensi Jenewa III","https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/gciii-1949/article-4"]," memberikan status tersebut kepada anggota angkatan bersenjata pihak yang berperang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedutaan Besar Ukraina di Jakarta ",["mengatakan","https://tirto.id/kedubes-ukraina-minta-wni-waspadai-tawaran-jadi-militer-rusia-hCjx"]," akan memberikan perlakuan manusiawi sesuai Konvensi Jenewa kepada warga asing yang ditangkap sebagai tawanan perang. Namun, mereka juga menyatakan orang yang secara sengaja dan sukarela bergabung dengan pasukan Rusia dapat menghadapi sanksi hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebuah ",["video yang viral","https://www.beritasatu.com/nasional/3024382/viral-wni-ditangkap-tentara-ukraina-klaim-dipaksa-jadi-tentara-rusia"]," pada 4 September memperlihatkan seorang laki-laki yang disebut WNI ditangkap pasukan Ukraina. Ia mengaku dipaksa menjadi tentara Rusia. Kasus seperti ini menunjukkan mengapa status seseorang tidak bisa disederhanakan menjadi satu label."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah, setidaknya hingga awal September, masih ",["menganggap mereka WNI","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5731661/yusril-verifikasi-wni-jadi-tentara-rusia-masih-berproses"],", dan Menteri Luar Negeri Sugiono ",["menyatakan","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5726871/soal-wni-jadi-tentara-rusia-menlu-berhak-dilindungi-selama-masih-wni"]," hak konsuler mereka tetap harus dipenuhi selama mereka masih berstatus WNI."]},{"k":"h","s":["Apa yang perlu dilakukan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ada empat hal yang bisa dilakukan untuk memperbaiki cara negara dan publik membicarakan kasus ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, media dan pejabat sebaiknya menggunakan istilah yang lebih netral, seperti ‘WNI di militer Rusia’ atau ‘WNI yang masuk dinas tentara asing’, selama status mereka belum terverifikasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, pemerintah perlu memverifikasi setiap kasus: apakah WNI tersebut resmi menjadi anggota angkatan bersenjata Rusia atau direkrut pihak lain di luar struktur militer. Menyebut mereka prajurit tidak berarti membenarkan keberadaan mereka di medan perang. Rusia mengisi barisannya dengan warga asing, yang sebagian ",["direkrut melalui tipu daya","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/international-and-comparative-law-quarterly/article/modern-slavery-in-armed-conflict-foreign-forced-fighters-in-ukraine/1D0028BC9208968FF6A5D50F0C26F008"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga, jika WNI tertangkap sebagai bagian dari pasukan Rusia, Kementerian Luar Negeri perlu segera meminta akses konsuler dan memastikan hak mereka sebagai tawanan perang terpenuhi sesuai hukum humaniter internasional."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keempat, penegakan hukum perlu menyasar para perekrut yang ",["menjaring WNI","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/09/01/19352281/wni-jadi-tentara-bayaran-rusia-guru-besar-ui-tak-dilindungi-hukum-humaniter"]," melalui tawaran pekerjaan palsu atau bergaji tinggi. Ada ",["ancaman pidana dalam KUHP","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5748464/duta-besar-ri-di-moskow-imbau-waspada-jebakan-tentara-bayaran"]," bagi pihak yang memengaruhi seseorang untuk menjadi tentara asing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah juga dapat meminta Moskow membuka data WNI yang telah menandatangani kontrak dengan militernya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Istilah ‘tentara bayaran’ memang mudah diucapkan dan terdengar tegas di ruang publik. Sayangnya, bagi WNI yang kini berada di medan perang, istilah yang sama bisa mempersempit perlindungan yang masih (dan seharusnya) dapat diupayakan oleh negara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Putin dicap penjahat perang: Menyoal wewenang dan standar ganda ICC – apa dampaknya bagi Rusia dan dunia?","https://theconversation.com/putin-dicap-penjahat-perang-menyoal-wewenang-dan-standar-ganda-icc-apa-dampaknya-bagi-rusia-dan-dunia-202615"]]}],"chars":7481},"https://theconversation.com/blocus-de-liran-pourquoi-larme-qui-a-fait-tomber-mossadegh-en-1953-ne-suffira-sans-doute-pas-aujourdhui-296571":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"f93f33b2b5ecabaf9a48590b919d2aa9c994cee8e0d0af7a6f3444baffa9f414","read":"https://theconversation.com/blocus-de-liran-pourquoi-larme-qui-a-fait-tomber-mossadegh-en-1953-ne-suffira-sans-doute-pas-aujourdhui-296571","bytes":188773,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Blocus de l’Iran : pourquoi l’arme qui a fait tomber Mossadegh en 1953 ne suffira sans doute pas aujourd’hui","by":[{"n":"Eric Lob","r":"Associate Professor of Politics and International Relations, Florida International University"}],"pub":"2026-11-14T08:49:08Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["Après la nationalisation de 1951, la production pétrolière iranienne a chuté d’environ 96 % sous le blocus et l’embargo britanniques."]},{"k":"li","s":["Dans cette crise, le premier ministre iranien Mossadegh n’a pas su réduire la pauvreté et a vu sa coalition éclater avant le putsch anglo-américain."]},{"k":"li","s":["Aujourd’hui, l’Iran répond à la pression américaine en perturbant le trafic des pétroliers et fait grimper les cours du brut."]},{"k":"p","s":["« Très peu de choses entrent en Iran, ou en sortent ! », a affirmé le président Donald Trump le 8 novembre 2026, ",["dans un message publié sur les réseaux sociaux","https://www.aljazeera.com/news-analysis/2026/11/9/trump-says-iran-is-sealed-off-but-can-new-us-task-force-stop-weapons-flow"]," où il vantait aussi « le plus grand blocus naval de l’histoire »."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ce message faisait suite à ",["l’annonce de la Task Force Iron Gate","https://www.centcom.mil/MEDIA/PUBLIC-RELEASES/Article/4644250/centcom-launches-task-force-to-disrupt-iranian-ground-transit-routes-supporting/"]," (une force opérationnelle du commandement militaire américain pour le Moyen-Orient, chargée de perturber les routes terrestres de l’Iran), dernier plan en date de l’administration Trump pour ",["isoler l’économie iranienne","https://theconversation.com/le-d-day-economique-au-moyen-orient-gagnants-et-perdants-290600"]," et contraindre ainsi le gouvernement de Téhéran à se plier à la volonté de Washington. Dans le même temps, Donald Trump a laissé entendre qu’un ",["retour à une guerre ouverte avec l’Iran était « hautement improbable »","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/08/trump-iran-strikes-unlikely-talks-hormuz.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["En ",["spécialiste des relations qu’entretient l’Iran","https://pir.fiu.edu/people/faculty-a-z/eric-lob1/eric-lob.html"]," avec le reste du monde, j’estime que la guerre menée par les États-Unis en Iran, qui entre dans son neuvième mois, ressemble de plus en plus à un épisode antérieur du conflit entre l’Iran et l’Occident. Au début des années 1950, les Britanniques ont ",["imposé à l’Iran un blocus et un embargo de deux ans","https://www.trumanlibrary.gov/library/online-collections/oil-crisis-in-iran"]," après que le premier ministre iranien de l’époque, Mohammad Mossadegh, eut nationalisé l’industrie pétrolière du pays, alors contrôlée par le Royaume-Uni."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces efforts ont abouti en 1953 à un complot, soutenu par les Britanniques et les Américains, qui visait à attiser la contestation en Iran et, ",["au bout du compte, à renverser Mossadegh","https://theconversation.com/iran-etats-unis-une-amitie-oubliee-130271"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Soixante-treize ans plus tard, bon nombre de ces thèmes (le pétrole, la coercition économique, l’ingérence politique) redeviennent d’actualité. Les ",["justifications fluctuantes","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/03/03/trump-iran-war-rationale-hegseth-rubio/"]," que Donald Trump avance pour cette guerre comprennent la neutralisation préventive d’une menace imminente et la non-prolifération nucléaire. Ses principales motivations semblent pourtant être de ",["choisir le dirigeant de l’Iran","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-says-he-wants-to-be-involved-in-picking-irans-next-leader"]," et de ",["contrôler son pétrole","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-threatens-to-take-total-control-of-irans-oil-industry-with-major-strikes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Faute d’y être parvenu par la force militaire directe, Donald Trump mise désormais avant tout sur un ",["blocus naval","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-iran-ports-blockade-strait-of-hormuz-trump/"]," et sur l’ ",["isolement économique","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-08-23/us-vows-economic-d-day-as-iran-threatens-to-halt-all-oil-exports"],", tout comme les Britanniques quelque sept décennies plus tôt."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mais l’analogie s’arrête peut-être là. Contrairement à l’époque de Mossadegh, l’Iran a montré qu’il pouvait riposter aux interventions étrangères et aux mesures de coercition économique par la ",["guerre asymétrique","https://www.rand.org/topics/asymmetric-warfare.html"]," et les perturbations économiques."]},{"k":"h","s":["De la nationalisation du pétrole…"]},{"k":"p","s":["En mars 1951, un mois avant de devenir premier ministre et alors qu’il siégeait comme député, Mossadegh ",["a convaincu le Parlement iranien","https://www.routledge.com/Social-Movements-in-Iran-Environmentalism-and-Civil-Society/Fadaee/p/book/9781138107748"],", le Majlis, d’adopter une loi qui nationalisait l’Anglo-Iranian Oil Company (la compagnie pétrolière britannique qui deviendra BP en 1954). Populaire auprès de nombreux Iraniens, qui y voyaient une mesure attendue de longue date pour reconquérir l’indépendance nationale et maîtriser les richesses du pays, cette décision ",["était considérée","https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691101347/iran-between-two-revolutions"]," par les Britanniques comme une rupture de contrat et comme le vol de leur plus important actif à l’étranger."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le Royaume-Uni ",["a déposé des plaintes auprès du tout jeune Conseil de sécurité des Nations unies","https://www.mohammadmossadegh.com/news/british-foreign-office/united-nations-iran-announcement/"],". Mais en juillet de la même année, les négociations se sont enlisées et les tensions se sont accrues entre Mossadegh, devenu entre-temps premier ministre, et les Britanniques."]},{"k":"p","s":["La coercition économique a commencé lorsque les Britanniques ont entravé les ventes de pétrole iranien en prévenant les pétroliers iraniens que leurs reçus, délivrés au moment du chargement de la cargaison, ne seraient pas acceptés sur le marché international. En août, le Royaume-Uni ",["a durci sa campagne en imposant","https://stephenkinzer.com/2013/09/all-the-shahs-men-an-american-coup-and-the-roots-of-middle-east-terror/"]," un blocus naval à l’Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les Britanniques ont alors intercepté des pétroliers au large des côtes persanes et empêché l’Iran d’exporter son pétrole vers d’autres pays. Ils ont aussi interdit l’exportation vers l’Iran de produits essentiels, comme le sucre et l’acier, et gelé les comptes bancaires et les avoirs iraniens au Royaume-Uni."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le même mois, le Royaume-Uni ",["a évacué ses techniciens britanniques et fermé les raffineries et d’autres installations de l’Anglo-Iranian Oil Company","https://press.syr.edu/supressbooks/261/mohammad-mosaddeq-and-the-1953-coup-in-iran/"]," à Abadan, dans le sud-ouest de l’Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mossadegh et son gouvernement pensaient pouvoir remplacer ces techniciens par d’autres, venus de l’étranger, tout en formant des Iraniens pour combler le vide. Mais, à force de menaces juridiques et d’accords, les Britanniques ont convaincu les autres compagnies pétrolières internationales, aux États-Unis et en Europe, à l’exception de l’Italie, de s’abstenir d’envoyer du personnel."]},{"k":"h","s":["… à l’opération Ajax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sous l’effet du blocus et de l’embargo britanniques, la production pétrolière iranienne ",["a chuté d’environ 96 %","https://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/oil-industry-ii/"]," et les revenus pétroliers du pays sont tombés quasiment à zéro entre 1950 et 1952. Dans le même temps, des compagnies pétrolières étrangères comme British Petroleum et Saudi Aramco (qui s’appelaient alors respectivement Anglo-Iranian Oil Company et Arabian American Oil Company) ",["ont doublé leur production","https://scholarship.law.vanderbilt.edu/vjtl/vol7/iss2/4/"]," pour compenser les conséquences économiques, pour le Royaume-Uni comme pour le reste du monde, d’une production et d’exportations iraniennes réduites, voire inexistantes."]},{"k":"p","s":["En pleine crise économique, l’incapacité de Mossadegh à faire reculer la pauvreté, entre autres problèmes, ",["a provoqué l’éclatement de sa coalition politique","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/international-journal-of-middle-east-studies/article/abs/1953-coup-detat-in-iran/A8025F967F0F09DE7F42939B47C6D7A4"]," et alimenté la campagne de propagande britannique et américaine menée contre lui jusqu’à ",["son renversement","https://theconversation.com/pourquoi-liran-se-mefie-t-il-autant-des-puissances-etrangeres-196736"]," lors de l’opération Ajax (nom de code du coup d’État orchestré par la CIA avec l’appui du MI6, les services secrets britanniques), le 19 août 1953."]},{"k":"p","s":["Un an plus tard, le chah d’Iran, Mohammad Reza Pahlavi (sur le trône de 1941 à 1979), a consolidé son pouvoir et ",["signé un accord pétrolier","https://archive.nytimes.com/www.nytimes.com/library/world/mideast/080654iran-statements.html"]," avec les Britanniques. Aux termes de cet accord, la part des bénéfices revenant à l’Iran augmentait légèrement, tandis qu’une écrasante majorité, comprise entre 75 % et 79 %, continuait d’aller aux compagnies britanniques et américaines. En échange, les Britanniques ont levé le blocus et permis à l’Iran de recommencer à exporter son pétrole sur le marché international."]},{"k":"h","s":["La dissuasion fait la différence"]},{"k":"p","s":["La campagne menée par le Royaume-Uni pour faire pression sur l’Iran et chasser son dirigeant présente des parallèles avec le conflit actuel. Aujourd’hui comme hier, une puissance occidentale espère mettre à genoux les dirigeants iraniens, et encourager de vastes manifestations contre le pouvoir, au moyen de mesures de coercition économique."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mais, contrairement aux années 1950, Téhéran est aujourd’hui mieux placé pour dissuader son adversaire étranger."]},{"k":"p","s":["Si Washington a considérablement ",["affaibli les capacités militaires conventionnelles de l’Iran","https://www.france24.com/en/us-claims-iran-s-missile-capabilities-severely-degraded"],", notamment son armée de l’air et sa marine, Téhéran a su recourir aux drones, aux missiles et à des groupes supplétifs pour frapper à maintes reprises des cibles américaines dans la région. Dans les années 1950, l’Iran ne disposait pas d’un réseau de milices régionales acquises à sa cause ",["comme celui qu’il possède aujourd’hui","https://theconversation.com/comment-liran-mobilise-son-axe-de-la-resistance-face-a-israel-216306"],", et il n’avait pas la technologie nécessaire pour riposter face à une armée supérieure sur le plan conventionnel."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’Iran peut aussi contrer les mesures économiques. Depuis le début de la guerre, en février 2026, Téhéran et ses partenaires ciblent sans relâche le trafic des pétroliers ainsi que les infrastructures civiles et énergétiques des États arabes du Golfe."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’Iran a ainsi ",["poussé les monarchies du Golfe à reconsidérer","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/10/gulf-states-rethink-security-us-israel-war-iran-ceasefire"]," leur maintien sous le parapluie sécuritaire américain et à ",["diversifier leurs partenariats de défense","https://carnegieendowment.org/middle-east/diwan/2026/08/the-mecca-agreement-unpacked"]," en s’ouvrant à d’autres puissances, dans la région et au-delà."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’Iran a également affirmé son contrôle, à des degrés divers, sur deux points de passage stratégiques, le ",["détroit d’Ormuz","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/attacks-tankers-hormuz-hit-highest-any-week-since-start-iran-war-sources-say-2026-10-07/"],", qui relie le golfe Persique au golfe d’Oman, et le ",["détroit de Bab el-Mandeb","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-09-10/saudi-says-no-danger-after-khamis-mushait-alert-amid-clashes-with-houthis"],", entre la mer Rouge et le golfe d’Aden, en coopération avec les ",["houthistes du Yémen","https://theconversation.com/pourquoi-il-est-errone-de-ne-voir-les-houthistes-que-comme-des-suppletifs-de-liran-294610"]," (un mouvement islamiste armé qui contrôle une partie du pays)."]},{"k":"p","s":["En attaquant les États arabes du Golfe et en perturbant la navigation commerciale dans la région, l’Iran ",["a fait grimper","https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/us-eia-hikes-oil-price-forecasts-again-iran-war-drains-global-stockpile-2026-10-06/"]," les prix du pétrole et d’autres matières premières, et exercé une pression économique et politique sur les États-Unis et d’autres pays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Et si les sanctions américaines et d’autres mesures ont aggravé les redoutables difficultés économiques que connaissait l’Iran avant la guerre ( ",["dévaluation record de la monnaie","https://apnews.com/article/iran-war-currency-hormuz-trump-91de6619aca2e1a9a32757166eae98d0"],", ",["inflation galopante","https://apnews.com/article/iran-war-blockade-medicine-pharmaceutical-prices-a66f60e950ec47b518a9a8856683ee75"]," et ",["contraction de la croissance","https://iranwire.com/en/features/158631-irans-economy-in-deep-recession-as-businesses-face-empty-malls-and-soaring-costs/"],"), le régime de Téhéran semble avoir surmonté les graves troubles sociaux ",["survenus juste avant le conflit","https://www.en-hrana.org/day-50-of-the-protests-intensification-of-security-prosecutions-and-uncertainty-regarding-the-status-of-detainees/"],", lors desquels des milliers de manifestants et d’autres citoyens sont descendus dans la rue et ont été tués par les forces de sécurité."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contrairement à Mossadegh, les dirigeants actuels de l’Iran ont eu des décennies pour se forger une capacité de résistance aux pressions extérieures. Et s’il a fallu deux ans de pression économique pour chasser Mossadegh du pouvoir, ",["des années de sanctions","https://theconversation.com/en-iran-les-sanctions-internationales-profitent-au-regime-129930"]," n’ont toujours pas réussi à mettre à genoux la République islamique d’Iran. Rien ne garantit qu’accentuer la pression aujourd’hui y change quoi que ce soit."]}],"chars":9328},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"062f39052e3534ed81d5381067a9631ce1db3ceceba34c675df6b6b0dabde243","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","bytes":74966,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Rwanda travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-11T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-04T10:15:14+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rusizi District"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the parts of Rusizi District which are within 10km of the border with the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), including the Rwandan islands in Lake Kivu and Kamembe Airport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rwanda-DRC border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Risks associated with the proximity of potential fighting in Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) may affect people on the Rwandan side of the border. International borders are often not well marked in remote areas, and you could unknowingly cross into DRC. You may see a presence of military personnel on both sides of the border."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Democratic Republic of the Congo’s travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"]," for more information. Keep up to date with developments through local media."]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings between Rwanda and DRC could close at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Rwanda’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Rwanda set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Rwandan High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Rwanda, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least one blank page for entry stamps."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Rwanda as a visitor. As a citizen of a Commonwealth country, you can get a free 30-day visa on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rwanda’s immigration department has information on ",["visa requirements","https://www.migration.gov.rw/our-services/visa-issued-under-special-arrangement"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["apply for a visa","https://www.rwandainuk.gov.rw/services/service-details/visa-application"]," from the Rwandan High Commission in London."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a ",["UK Police Certificate","https://www.acro.police.uk/s/"]," before you travel if you’re applying for a resident, business or missionary multiple-entry visa. It usually takes at least 10 working days to process."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of the Congo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Land border crossing opening hours between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) at Gisenyi-Goma and Cyangugu-Bukavu vary. The conflict in DRC could further affect border crossings (see ",["Democratic Republic of the Congo’s travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"],"). The FCDO currently advises against all but essential travel to parts of the Rusizi District."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may experience immigration difficulties if you do not have residency status and regularly cross between the two countries."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border measures"]},{"k":"p","s":["In response to the current Ebola outbreak in DRC, the Government of Rwanda has introduced ",["health-screening measures at Kigali International Airport and border restrictions with DRC","https://www.rbc.gov.rw/PHSEPR/about-ebola-2/"],". These measures may be subject to short notice change. Check the latest advice of local authorities and tour operators ahead of travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Rwanda","https://www.rra.gov.rw/en/customs-services/travelers/prohibited-goods"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare drones when you arrive. They may be confiscated or held until you leave the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Rwanda, if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],", you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Rwanda guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/187/rwanda#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Rwanda cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are relatively low in Rwanda, but there are cases of burglary, theft, bag-snatching and mugging (violent theft) in Kigali."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when walking at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["arrange transport in advance"]},{"k":"li","s":["lock car doors when driving"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave valuables in parked cars"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying large amounts of money or other valuables"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal safety in military zones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some off-limits military zones in Kigali may not be well lit or signposted. You could be arrested and detained if you enter these areas. Take extra care when walking around less populated zones, particularly at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Rwanda have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to photograph some government buildings. If you use a drone to take photographs of a prohibited area without a permit, you risk being imprisoned or receiving a severe fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consensual same-sex sexual acts are not illegal in Rwanda, but can be frowned upon by locals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rwanda’s laws do not discriminate against sexual orientation, and its constitution prohibits all forms of discrimination. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Plastic bag ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a ban on plastic bags in Rwanda for environmental reasons. If you have plastic bags when you arrive in the country, they will be confiscated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vaporisers, e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vapes and e-cigarettes are banned in Rwanda. It is illegal to bring them into the country, including for personal use. If you are found in possession of vapes or e-cigarettes you will have them confiscated and could be fined."]},{"k":"h","s":["Genocide Memorial Day"]},{"k":"p","s":["The week following Genocide Memorial Day on 7 April is an official week of mourning."]},{"k":"h","s":["National day of community service (Umuganda)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The last Saturday of each month is Umuganda, a national day of community service. Most normal services close from 7am to 11am. Kigali also has a car-free morning from 7am to 10am on the first and third Sunday of the month to promote exercise and reduce car emissions. Other cities in the country may also hold car-free mornings. You should check with the local authorities as these might happen at different times."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gorilla and Chimpanzee trekking"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to travel close to the Democratic Republic of the Congo border on a gorilla or chimpanzee trek, check travel advice for ",["Rusizi District and the DRC border region","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda"],". If you plan on crossing the border into DRC, ",["check the travel advice for DRC","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/democratic-republic-of-the-congo"],". Short-notice border closures could impact any travel plans in the region. Plan your journey in advance and discuss your itinerary with your tour operator. Keep up to date with developments through your tour operator and check the local media."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Rwanda, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["After one year of driving, you must have a Rwandan licence. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["write a letter of application to the Commissioner Traffic and Road Safety"]},{"k":"li","s":["attach your existing licence"]},{"k":"li","s":["attach a copy of your visa or foreign resident ID card"]},{"k":"li","s":["pay a fee"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads from Kigali to all major towns are in good condition but can be damaged by landslides during the rainy season. After dark, many roads outside of larger urban centres are unlit and driving standards are poor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shared taxis (mini vans) and motorbike taxis are the most common form of public transport, but are very vulnerable to accidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Building health and safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Levels of building health and safety in Rwanda are lower than in the UK. Buildings and construction sites have collapsed, causing deaths and serious injuries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire safety standards vary and fires in residential and public places are a continuing risk. Poor wiring and sub-standard electrical cables have caused building fires. Take extra care when using electronic equipment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season runs from February to May and from September to December. April is the height of the rainy season. Heavy storms can cause disruption and damage, including landslides and floods. Monitor local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes in Rwanda. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],". The US Geological Survey has a real-time earthquake map that ",["captures information following significant seismic activity","https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/map/?extent=-13.71004,11.64551&extent=9.0587,51.72363"],". If there is an earthquake, monitor local media reports and follow the advice of the authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rwanda-DRC border"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for the Rwanda-DRC border on the Warnings and insurance page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rwanda-Burundi border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Burundi closed the border to Rwanda in January 2024. There might be some tension near the border, as both sides have accused the other of cross-border raids targeting local inhabitants."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rwanda-Uganda border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossings Uganda have temporarily closed at short notice in recent years. Be aware of the impact that short-notice border closures could have on any travel plans in the region."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cross-border additional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling near the DRC or Burundi borders, be aware of the risk of cross-border attacks and government security operations given the ongoing conflict in eastern DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent years, armed incursions have occurred into south-west Rwanda:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 18 June 2023, 2 people were killed and 6 were injured when suspected militants opened fire on a public passenger bus on Nyamagabe-Rusizi road, in Nyungwe Forest, Nyamgabe District"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 17 June 2023, a Congolese soldier crossed into Rwanda at Gisenyi and fired on civilians and Rwandan security personnel near the border, injuring 2 Rwandan police officers – the soldier was shot dead"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, artillery fire from the DRC hit Rwandan territory, close to the border in Kinigi sector of Musanze District in the north-west"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest information on ",["recommended vaccinations","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/187/rwanda#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Rwanda","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/187/rwanda#General_Information"]," including mpox."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Rwanda. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 15 May the Democratic Republic of Congo Ministry of Health announced an outbreak of Ebola Bundibugyo in the North-Eastern Ituri Province. Read more about the ",["Ebola outbreak on TravelHealth Pro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/63/democratic-republic-of-the-congo#Outbreaks"]," and see ",["information on Ebola and similar diseases.","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/68/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"]," World Health Organisation (WHO) have ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the outbreak, you may experience heightened health screening at international borders in the region. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Marburg virus disease (MVD)"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 20 December 2024, the Government of Rwanda announced the end of the outbreak of Marburg virus disease that began on 27 September 2024. The outbreak was linked to contact with fruit bats in a mine near Kigali."]},{"k":"p","s":["The last confirmed case of Marburg virus disease was reported on 30 October 2024. There remains a risk of re-emergence of the disease linked to viral persistence in body fluids of recovered patients and the potential animal reservoir in the country, so if visiting or working in caves inhabited by fruit bat colonies, you should wear gloves and other appropriate protective clothing (including face masks)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the latest situation with local authorities before travelling. You can find more information on Marburg virus disease from the ",["WHO","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/marburg-virus-disease"],", and ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/799/marburg-virus-disease-in-rwanda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only limited medical facilities are available in Rwanda. If you have a serious accident or illness, you may need to be evacuated by air ambulance to Kenya or South Africa."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rwanda-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/living-in-rwanda-guidance/living-in-rwanda-guidance#healthcare-in-rwanda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Rwanda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 111"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Rwanda"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Rwanda"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Rwanda"]," in Rwanda"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rwanda-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rwanda-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/rwanda/british-high-commission-kigali"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Rwanda","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-rwanda"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17287,"change":"New information about vapes and e-cigarette bans in Rwanda and updated information about border measures introduced by the Rwandan Government in response to the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo ('Entry requirements' and 'Safety and security' pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"76ba6b49e3a6664472a0e2527ceb19feecbb4291024d864030d1cb0db7ad7b69","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia","bytes":81358,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Tunisia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-24T17:07:53+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Western Tunisia, including the Tunisia-Algeria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Chaambi Mountains National Park"]},{"k":"li","s":["the designated military operations zones: Mount Salloum"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Sammamma"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Mghila"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to cross-border terrorist activity and operations by the Tunisian security forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas north and west of the town of Ghardimaou in Jendouba Governorate, including El Feidja National Park"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 20km of the Tunisia-Algeria border in El Kef and Jendouba governorates, south of the town of Jendouba"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kasserine Governorate, including the town of Sbeitla"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 10km of the rest of the Tunisia-Algeria border south of Kasserine Governorate"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 10km of Mount Mghila"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Orbata"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Southern Tunisia, including the Tunisia-Libya border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the militarised zone south of the towns of El Borma and Dhehiba"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 20km of the rest of the Tunisia-Libya border area north of Dhehiba"]},{"k":"li","s":["the town of Ben Guerdane and immediate surrounding area"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to cross-border terrorist activity and fighting in Libya."]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 75km of the Tunisia-Libya border, including Remada and El Borma but excluding Zarzis, the C118 road and all areas in Medenine Governorate north of the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide and any specific travel advice that applies to you:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["disabled travellers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["volunteering and adventure travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Tunisia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Tunisian Embassy in the UK","https://consular.website/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tunisia, your passport should be valid for the duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Damaged or torn passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Tunisia with a damaged or torn passport, you may encounter difficulties when attempting to leave the country. Ensure your passport is in good condition before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Tunisian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual British-Tunisian nationals should enter and leave Tunisia on the same passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Tunisia without a visa for up to 90 days, except for holders of Crown Dependency passports, who may need to buy a visa on arrival. Contact the ",["Tunisian Embassy in the UK","https://consular.website/"]," for information on how to apply."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials will stamp your passport on arrival and check the length of your stay on departure. If you overstay the 90-day period without a valid reason, you will have to pay a fine. You can pay on departure at the airport, or in advance at some police stations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["On arrival in Tunisia, border officials have the right to ask for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your contact details"]},{"k":"li","s":["your onward or return travel tickets"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of a hotel booking or other accommodation details"]},{"k":"p","s":["A small number of visitors have been denied entry to Tunisia, or been delayed, for not being able to provide sufficient evidence of accommodation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Additional processing at airports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials check passenger names against an immigration database. A small number of passengers with the same or similar names to those on the database have been delayed and questioned on arrival and departure to confirm their identity. Occasionally border officials carry out searches on these passengers. Statistically, this has disproportionately affected British nationals of South Asian descent."]},{"k":"p","s":["This can cause distress and inconvenience. The British Embassy in Tunis cannot override decisions made by the Tunisian authorities but if you are affected, contact the British Embassy on +216 71 108 700 or contact the Tunisian Embassy in London."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hotel tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to pay a hotel tax upon arrival. This tax amounts to 8 Tunisian Dinars per person per night for 3-star hotels and 12 Tunisian Dinars per person per night for 4- and 5-star hotels. The tax is charged for a maximum of ten nights, so guests staying longer will only pay for the first ten nights of their stay. The tax cannot be reclaimed if you leave early."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Tunisia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/226/tunisia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Tunisia","https://www.douane.gov.tn/prohibitions-et-restrictions/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Tunisia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tunisia has strict currency controls. If you are bringing foreign currency into Tunisia, including pound sterling, check the ",["applicable rules","https://www.douane.gov.tn/devises-et-change/"]," and whether you need to make a declaration on arrival. Failure to declare foreign currency may result in confiscation. Keep declaration documents. You are not allowed to take Tunisian dinars out of Tunisia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep official exchange receipts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring drones into Tunisia without authorisation. Any drones detected will be confiscated and stored until your departure."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["Certain electronic devices with recording, transmission or smart-function capabilities may be subject to restrictions, or be confiscated on arrival for the duration of your visit. If you intend to travel with devices such as Ray-Ban Meta Smart Glasses or walkie-talkies, including toy ones, check the latest requirements with the Tunisian authorities before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Tunisia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Tunisia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Tunisia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security forces remain on a high state of alert in Tunis and other places. You may be at higher risk in and around:"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites, tourist sites and festivals"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["public transport networks and vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["businesses with western interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas where foreign nationals and tourists are known to gather, or any crowded area"]},{"k":"p","s":["The terrorism threat comes from both established groups and self-initiated individuals."]},{"k":"p","s":["A formal state of emergency has been in place since a terrorist attack against a police bus took place in 2015. The security forces are visibly present in many parts of the country, including at the entry points to some towns and cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite some improvements in border security, there remains continuing instability and violence on the border with Libya. Tunisian security forces have been the primary target in terrorist-related incidents, mainly in border areas including in the Chaambi Mountains. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023 a number of terrorist attacks were planned and carried out by self-initiated individuals possibly influenced by terrorist organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, a National Guard officer was stabbed in the Goulette area of Tunis"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, a police officer was stabbed and killed outside the Brazilian Embassy in Tunis"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, a fatal shooting took place on the island of Djerba, at a Jewish pilgrimage site, with 3 security personnel and 2 civilians killed, and 10 injured"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, 2 security officers were injured in a knife attack near a synagogue in central Tunis"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2021, police shot and wounded an assailant who attacked them with a knife and axe in front of the Interior Ministry in central Tunis"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020, a suicide bombing targeting a police patrol in Tunis killed one police officer and injured 4 others"]},{"k":"li","s":["in June 2015, 38 foreign tourists were killed, including 30 British nationals, in a terrorist attack at Port El Kantaoui near Sousse"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March 2015, 21 tourists were killed, including a British national, in a terrorist attack at the Bardo Museum in the centre of Tunis"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["In response to the current situation in Israel and Palestine, peaceful demonstrations have occurred in some Tunisian cities, including outside some western embassies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations and protests happen occasionally and may start with little or no warning. Although rare, they can sometimes become violent. Demonstrations and protests tend to be at weekends and on prominent national dates (which may include 14 January and 17 December). They usually take place in central areas of Tunis and other major cities, and may focus on government buildings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labour strikes and industrial action can cause disruption to public transport, airports, seaports and road networks. Land border crossings may have delays or temporary closures."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities may impose curfews or set up checkpoints at short notice in response to events. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid demonstrations, protests and strikes wherever possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["move away from areas where demonstrations are taking place"]},{"k":"li","s":["obey curfews and other instructions given by the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor events through the media and follow the advice of your hotel and tour operator"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Migration from sub-Saharan Africa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large numbers of irregular migrants depart from Tunisia for Europe. Many migrants in Tunisia originate from sub-Saharan African countries. This has resulted in heightened social tensions, and anti-migrant protests and violence in some coastal towns, such as Sfax. Incidents could happen with little or no warning and might affect anyone perceived to be of sub-Saharan African origin."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of visits to Tunisia are unaffected by crime. The most common crime experienced is theft. Sensible measures to reduce this risk include not displaying expensive items or leaving them unattended, and not carrying unnecessary valuables when in public. Criminals are known to sometimes use confidence tricks as a distraction while carrying out thefts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual harassment and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Reports of sexual harassment and sexual assault statistically increase in the summer months. Reports include trouble in busy public places at night and quieter public parks and beaches during the daytime."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a foreign national, you must carry ID, such as a copy of the photo page of your passport. Security officials may ask you for ID at any time. Dual British-Tunisian nationals should carry a copy of the photo page of their passport or their national ID card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beach-appropriate clothing in holiday resorts is acceptable, however when visiting religious sites or remote areas of the country, local custom is to dress modestly."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country, next starting in February 2027. During this time, eating or drinking, smoking or chewing gum in public in the daytime may cause offence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts. You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that hotels and restaurants serving food or drink in fasting hours may separate you from Muslim guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["The sale of alcohol is permitted in Tunisia but is banned from sale in supermarkets on Fridays. You can still order and drink alcohol in hotels and bars. During Ramadan, sale of alcohol is banned and the consumption of alcohol is restricted to fewer restaurants and bars. These rules do not apply at holiday resorts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drugs and illegal substances"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring any controlled or prohibited substances into Tunisia. Travellers found in possession of illegal drugs can face severe penalties, including lengthy prison sentences and heavy fines. Tunisian legislation relating to illegal drugs applies regardless of the traveller’s country of residence, country of departure, whether the substance is legal elsewhere or the quantity being carried. Do not carry any such substances into the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photographs of or near government buildings or military sites."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying antiquities"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get permission from the Tunisian authorities before removing antiquities from Tunisia. Not getting permission in advance can result in lengthy delays on departure. If you do not declare the item, you could get a fine and a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying property"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for foreign nationals to buy property outright in Tunisia. British nationals often do this through a Tunisian third party. If you are considering buying property, consult a local lawyer. Do not make private arrangements, which may be illegal and could result in a large financial loss."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Tunisia. Members of the LGBT+ community have been targeted by criminals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some beaches have a flag system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children, even if they can swim or there’s a lifeguard present. Take extra care and get local advice if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad bikes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Quad bikes are popular in desert resorts. Take the same precautions as you would in the UK. Safety standards can vary considerably. Always wear a crash helmet."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Tunisia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Tunisia for up to one year with a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. You also need to carry a ",["green card","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," to prove you have the minimum insurance cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Tunisia, and the legal limit in Tunisia is stricter than for England and Wales. If you are tested and found to be above the limit, you could get a fine and a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road surfaces are of a reasonable standard in Tunisia, although large potholes can appear after heavy rain. Many towns and villages have unannounced speed bumps. Be careful when approaching sand drifts on roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving at night can be hazardous outside towns, due to unlit roads, vehicles without lights and livestock on the road. Check the availability of petrol stations with local drivers before travelling long distances in remote areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards can be low. Vehicles entering roundabouts or junctions do not always follow the established right of way. Lane discipline can be poor. Pay particular attention when approaching traffic lights, especially at night, as other drivers may not obey the signals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pedestrians tend to walk on the roads and they have the right of way."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may come across military or police security checkpoints. Approach slowly and do not cross without permission. Be prepared to present ID and driving licence if asked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rail travel is generally safe, although safety standards tend to be lower than in the UK. There is a risk of petty crime on trains."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Power supply in summer months"]},{"k":"p","s":["In summer months, heatwaves and extreme temperatures may occur. This can cause an increase in the pressure on the electricity grid. In response, the Tunisian electricity and gas company (STEG) may carry out temporary power cuts. These disruptions can have a direct impact on infrastructure across the country, including in some hotels. Power cuts can temporarily affect air conditioning, mobile phone networks and Internet connections. In extreme cases cuts can impact water supply and payment transactions (ATMs and card payments). Disruptions are usually only temporary. Find out more from your tour operator, at your accommodation or via local media regarding potential restrictions in your area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Tunisia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Western Tunisia, including the Tunisia-Algeria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Chaambi Mountains National Park"]},{"k":"li","s":["the designated military operations zones: Mount Salloum"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Sammamma"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Mghila"]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas north and west of the town of Ghardimaou in Jendouba Governorate, including El Feidja National Park"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 20km of the Tunisia-Algeria border in El Kef and Jendouba governorates, south of the town of Jendouba, including the archaeological site of Chemtou"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kasserine Governorate, including the town of Sbeitla"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 10km of the rest of the Tunisia-Algeria border south of Kasserine Governorate"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 10km of Mount Mghila"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mount Orbata"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened Tunisian security presence at the border with Algeria. See ",["Algeria travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/algeria"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Southern Tunisia, including the Tunisia-Libya border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the militarised zone south of the towns of El Borma and Dhehiba"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 20km of the rest of the Tunisia-Libya border area north of Dhehiba"]},{"k":"li","s":["the town of Ben Guerdane and immediate surrounding area"]},{"k":"p","s":["In addition, FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 75km of the Tunisia-Libya border, including Remada and El Borma but excluding Zarzis, the C118 road and all areas in Medenine Governorate north of the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened Tunisian security presence at the border with Libya due to cross-border terrorist activity and fighting in Libya. Border crossings are sometimes closed temporarily without notice. Some violent incidents have occurred. See ",["Libya travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/libya"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 190 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Tunisia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/226/tunisia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Tunisia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/226/tunisia"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re bringing prescription medicines, keep them in the original packaging and carry a note from your GP confirming the medication has been prescribed to you. If you have any specific concerns about taking certain types of medication with you to Tunisia, contact the ",["Tunisian Embassy in the UK","https://consular.website/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Tunisia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["list of medical providers in Tunisia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tunisia-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak some English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s no provision for free medical attention for foreign nationals in Tunisia. All doctors’ fees, medication and treatment in private clinics must be paid for on the spot (and sometimes before treatment). These costs can be high. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Tunisia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 190"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire and car accidents: 198"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police (when in towns and cities): 197"]},{"k":"p","s":["National Guard (when in rural areas and small villages): 193"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking lawyers and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Tunisia"]," in Tunisia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Tunisia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-tunisia/bereavement-information-pack-tunisia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Tunisia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tunisia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/tunisia/british-embassy-tunis"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tunisia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Tunisia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-tunisia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23071,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy with changes made throughout, including visa requirements, taking money into and out of Tunisia, electronic devices, drugs and illegal substances and power supply in summer months ('Entry requirements' and 'Safety and security') pages."}};
